 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+For moving tickets in from another tracker.
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [ { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com", "priority": "high" }, { "...": "..." } ] }
+```
+
+Each item is what `POST /tickets` takes, and at most 5000 items. The tickets are created in the order given, each recorded
+and its requester notified exactly as when one ticket is created (the actor of every audit entry is the `X-Actor`).
+Answers 201 with `{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0043", "T-0044"] }`, the ids in the order of the items.
+
+All or none: when any item is invalid, or the list holds more than 5000, nothing is created and the answer is 400
+`invalid`; the message names the first invalid item by its index in the array, `0` for the first
+(`tickets[2]: priority must be one of low, normal, high, urgent`). The body may be larger than `MAX_BODY_BYTES`, which
+still limits the other endpoints.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
 | Parameter | Meaning |
